& [ReportForm] is exact and deterministic
  + [CTM-001] CoordinationTransportMeasurement is a strict versioned JSON form
  + [CTM-002] it records fixture source tool name static metrics ordered schedule metrics findings nonclaims and report digest
  + [CTM-003] report_digest is canonical SHA-256 over compact JSON with only report_digest cleared
  + [CTM-004] pretty artifact emission has a single trailing newline and equal runs are byte-identical

& [Fixture] uses production admission
  + [CTM-005] the checked cppe_two_process_candidate fixture is assigned measurement-specific candidate author evidence invocation session and frame identities
  + [CTM-006] run_authorship_lane constructs the exact successful lane and CoordinationToolContext projection
  + [CTM-007] all dispatch uses execute_coordination_tool_request and no checkpoint response or byte count is fabricated

& [StaticMetrics] isolate fixed values
  + [CTM-008] record compact UTF-8 JSON bytes for context BEGIN request BEGIN response and genesis checkpoint
  + [CTM-009] record compact JSON bytes for complete MCP tool metadata input schema and output schema
  + [CTM-010] all byte counts use serde_json::to_vec on the named public value

& [ScheduleMetrics] cover coarse and fine chunking
  + [CTM-011] ordered quotas are one two four eight and sixty-four
  + [CTM-012] every schedule includes one BEGIN call and repeatedly ADVANCEs its successor checkpoint until terminal
  + [CTM-013] each schedule records total calls advance calls steps total request bytes total response bytes total structured bytes maximum request and response bytes and minimum maximum and aggregate checkpoint bytes
  + [CTM-014] the uninterrupted lane's exact terminal step count is recorded and every schedule must reach the same terminal CoordinationOutcome after that count
  + [CTM-015] terminal outcome bytes and SHA-256 digest are recorded and equal across schedules

& [ContextMetrics] state only arithmetic ceilings
  + [CTM-016] repeated_context_bytes equals context_bytes multiplied by call_count because every request carries context once
  + [CTM-017] zero_byte_handle_upper_bound equals context_bytes multiplied by call_count minus one
  + [CTM-018] context shares are integer basis points with floor division and no floating-point instability
  + [CTM-019] the upper bound assumes a zero-byte handle and therefore cannot be claimed as realizable savings

& [Validation] fails closed
  + [CTM-020] zero missing duplicate or unexpected quota schedules fail report validation
  + [CTM-021] inconsistent arithmetic checkpoint ranges step totals terminal bytes digest or report digest fail validation
  + [CTM-022] a checked artifact must equal fresh generated pretty JSON byte for byte

& [Boundary] is one fixture byte account
  + [CTM-023] no elapsed-time allocation RSS tokenization context-window model-quality provider throughput or network measurement is included
  + [CTM-024] no general-program extrapolation registry implementation custody persistence authentication host registration model call or external effect is authorized

& [Acceptance] is finite
  + [CTM-A01] source SJS signature and seven-fold trace verify
  + [CTM-A02] equal report generation and digest validation pass
  + [CTM-A03] all five schedules terminate at the recorded fixture step count with one exact outcome and valid arithmetic
  + [CTM-A04] checked artifact equals fresh output and supports a bounded registry decision
  + [CTM-A05] formatting warnings-denied lint focused and workspace regression manifest audit narrative and scoped Git review pass

